{"name":"Elote","hex":"#ffe8ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elote","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Corn (maize) harvested before reaching full maturity.","A street food dish originating in Central America, but now also popular in the United States, consisting of corn on the cob which is grilled or boiled and served on a stick, typically with toppings such as cheese, chili powder, mayonnaise, and lime juice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elote"}],"entries":[{"title":"Corn on the cob","blocks":[{"text":"Corn on the cob is a culinary term for a cooked ear of sweet corn (maize) eaten directly off the cob. Variations of the corn on the cob include the Masala Bhutta in India, Yaki-tōmorokoshi in Japan and Elote in Latin American countries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/CookedCornOnTheCob.JPG/330px-CookedCornOnTheCob.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corn_on_the_cob","wikidata":"Q5171058"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Corn_on_the_cob_%28Clovis%2C_Ca_2022%29.png/250px-Corn_on_the_cob_%28Clovis%2C_Ca_2022%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/87/Corn_on_the_cob_%28Clovis%2C_Ca_2022%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Corn_on_the_cob_%28Clovis%2C_Ca_2022%29.png/250px-Corn_on_the_cob_%28Clovis%2C_Ca_2022%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACorn_on_the_cob_(Clovis%2C_Ca_2022).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/LoikawCorn.jpg/500px-LoikawCorn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1